Notes on the platform choices baked in:
- No in-page back arrow or sticky footer button — `BackButton`/`MainButton` own those spots; a second control would collide with the host's.
- `showConfirm`/`showAlert` instead of `window.confirm`/`alert`, since the browser versions are blocked or look foreign in several Telegram clients.
- Every color is a `--tg-theme-*` CSS variable with a sane fallback for plain-browser testing outside Telegram.
- `isVersionAtLeast` gates the newer APIs (`setBottomBarColor`, `disableVerticalSwipes`, `hideKeyboard`) so older clients degrade gracefully instead of throwing.
